{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00058",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 7.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.04,
      "end_seconds": 12.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.11,
      "end_seconds": 18.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Uh, um, good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.46,
      "end_seconds": 23.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Right, of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.01,
      "end_seconds": 32.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Honestly, it's fever and chills, and my family pushed me to come. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.37,
      "end_seconds": 35.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.36,
      "end_seconds": 49.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.71,
      "text": "It's been one week now. I did try to ignore it for a while. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.81,
      "end_seconds": 53.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Anything that helps?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.21,
      "end_seconds": 59.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Right, I get some relief from paracetamol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.85,
      "end_seconds": 65.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "What about sharp pain on the right side when you breathe in, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.47,
      "end_seconds": 74.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Yeah. About a week, I'd say. I've had a cough with phlegm too, for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.49,
      "end_seconds": 77.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Any palpitations or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.58,
      "end_seconds": 80.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.63,
      "end_seconds": 83.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Any recent travel or confusion at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.49,
      "end_seconds": 86.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.67,
      "end_seconds": 89.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Right. And leg swelling, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.41,
      "end_seconds": 91.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Well, no leg swelling, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.24,
      "end_seconds": 93.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "What about vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.86,
      "end_seconds": 95.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No vomiting, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 98.95,
      "end_seconds": 102.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice vomiting. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.46,
      "end_seconds": 108.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.37,
      "end_seconds": 117.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Okay, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.42,
      "end_seconds": 120.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.9,
      "end_seconds": 123.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.86,
      "end_seconds": 125.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 128.05,
      "end_seconds": 138.59,
      "duration_seconds": 10.54,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. SpO2 94 percent on room air, temperature is 37.0 degrees, pressure 127 over 89. Heart rate 96, respiratory rate 21."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.39,
      "end_seconds": 140.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.25,
      "end_seconds": 143.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.04,
      "end_seconds": 145.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.85,
      "end_seconds": 161.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.46,
      "end_seconds": 165.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "My father had kidney stones. My father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.75,
      "end_seconds": 170.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.15,
      "end_seconds": 179.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "I'm on metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. Tiotropium inhaler, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.01,
      "end_seconds": 180.78,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.51,
      "end_seconds": 186.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "I take Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 186.82,
      "end_seconds": 191.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 1300 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.67,
      "end_seconds": 197.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.34,
      "end_seconds": 201.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.94,
      "end_seconds": 203.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.38,
      "end_seconds": 208.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Just a lump removed from my back, years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.65,
      "end_seconds": 212.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.37,
      "end_seconds": 217.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Yes, penicillin, it gives me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.12,
      "end_seconds": 221.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.59,
      "end_seconds": 227.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. Yeah, yes, COPD. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.64,
      "end_seconds": 231.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.15,
      "end_seconds": 234.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.99,
      "end_seconds": 239.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.3,
      "end_seconds": 243.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.3,
      "end_seconds": 264.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "There's bronchial breathing and crackles at the right lower zone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.69,
      "end_seconds": 266.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.7,
      "end_seconds": 269.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.13,
      "end_seconds": 287.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Breathing rate is a bit fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.96,
      "end_seconds": 296.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.05,
      "end_seconds": 300.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "I mean, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.76,
      "end_seconds": 312.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.29,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is a possible pneumonia on the right side. It could also be a pulmonary embolism, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.6,
      "end_seconds": 318.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "I've, I've been thinking the worst, you know, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.59,
      "end_seconds": 335.4,
      "duration_seconds": 15.81,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a possible pneumonia on the right side is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had fever and chills for one week, and no palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.64,
      "end_seconds": 339.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.32,
      "end_seconds": 343.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.56,
      "end_seconds": 345.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.3,
      "end_seconds": 368.8,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. I'd like to arrange a sputum culture for pneumonia. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 369.95,
      "end_seconds": 375.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Doctor, I did a chest X-ray before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.56,
      "end_seconds": 405.48,
      "duration_seconds": 28.92,
      "text": "Okay, thanks, I'll look at that. I'd like you to take levofloxacin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for five days. That's for chest infection. Rest and fluids, and finish every dose of the antibiotic. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 406.93,
      "end_seconds": 408.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Okay, uh, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.54,
      "end_seconds": 418.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "If the breathlessness worsens or you become drowsy, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.18,
      "end_seconds": 420.88,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 421.9,
      "end_seconds": 428.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "Come back after the X-ray. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.97,
      "end_seconds": 438.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "So, I take the levofloxacin, 500 milligrams, once a day and come back after the X-ray. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.93,
      "end_seconds": 443.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.41,
      "end_seconds": 449.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Right, that's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.87,
      "end_seconds": 450.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}